OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sat 3 Oct to Mon 12 Oct
OL,6,FHigh pressure will likely be in place
OL,7,Facross much of central and southern UK
OL,8,Fthrough the first few days of this
OL,9,Fperiod. This means plenty of dry
OL,10,Fweather to be had, albeit with some
OL,11,Fchilly nights and overnight and
OL,12,Fmorning fog in places. In the north, a
OL,13,Frather more changeable pattern will
OL,14,Fcontinue, with occasional rain and
OL,15,Foften breezier conditions. Towards the
OL,16,Fend of this period, high pressure may
OL,17,Fhave declined somewhat, allowing lower
OL,18,Fpressure to become rather more
OL,19,Fdominant, this probably centred
OL,20,Fsomewhere to the west or south of the
OL,21,FUK, though its proximity to the UK is
OL,22,Fmore uncertain. However, there is a
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fchance of some rain developing across
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fparts of the south by mid-month.
OL,25,FOverall, temperatures remaining above
OL,26,Faverage overall.
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
SC,0003
CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1790605124
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Tue 13 Oct to Tue 27 Oct
OL,6,FQuite an uncertain period of weather,
OL,7,Fwith earlier signals of reliably
OL,8,Fwetter than normal weather now looking
OL,9,Fless likely. That being said, the
OL,10,Fmiddle of the month could be a quite a
OL,11,Fchangeable period of weather overall,
OL,12,Fwith the wettest weather most likely
OL,13,Ftowards parts of the west and possibly
OL,14,Fsouth. It is quite plausible that
OL,15,Fmarked regional variation in rainfall
OL,16,Famounts will occur. Temperatures are
OL,17,Flikely to remain broadly above average
OL,18,Foverall.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
